<Layout title="TBS Fusion Pico Interface Research — CopperTrace" description="Investigating computer control of a TBS Fusion analogue FPV receiver with a Raspberry Pi Pico.">
<article class="article"><div class="article-meta">Project 004 · Active investigation</div><h1>TBS Fusion + Pico interface research</h1>
<p class="lead">An investigation into using a Raspberry Pi Pico as an interface to a TBS Fusion analogue FPV receiver, with the longer-term goal of integrating a higher-quality receiver into an Ethernet-connected sensing node.</p>
<div class="callout"><strong>Status: under investigation.</strong> The internal Fusion interface and connector mapping have not yet been fully verified on this bench. This page deliberately separates established hardware facts from the proposed control architecture.</div>
<h2>Why Fusion?</h2><p>Simple RX5808 modules are useful for inexpensive scanning nodes, but Fusion provides a more capable analogue receiver platform. A controllable Fusion interface would allow its behaviour to be compared with the existing dual-RX5808 architecture while keeping the surrounding Ethernet and evidence pipeline unchanged.</p>
<h2>Proposed architecture</h2><div class="diagram"><div class="diagram-title">INVESTIGATION TARGET</div><div class="diagram-row"><div class="diagram-node">TBS Fusion receiver</div></div><div class="diagram-arrow">↓</div><div class="diagram-row"><div class="diagram-node diagram-accent">Pico interface layer</div></div><div class="diagram-arrow">↓</div><div class="diagram-row diagram-split"><div class="diagram-node">Receiver control</div><div class="diagram-node">Measurements / status</div></div><div class="diagram-arrow">↓</div><div class="diagram-row"><div class="diagram-node">Ethernet sensing infrastructure</div></div></div>
<h2>What is established</h2><p>The available Fusion hardware includes receiver modules and spare bottom boards suitable for bench investigation. The existing analogue sensing work already provides the surrounding Pico/Ethernet architecture against which a Fusion-based approach can be evaluated.</p>
<h2>What still needs measurement</h2><ul><li>Map connector pins and verify voltage levels before attaching GPIO.</li><li>Identify control and status signals with a logic analyser.</li><li>Determine whether channel/frequency control can be reproduced safely from a Pico.</li><li>Capture known UI actions and correlate them with bus activity.</li><li>Compare scan behaviour and usable measurements with the dual-RX5808 node.</li></ul>
<h2>Publication rule</h2><p>No pinout or protocol will be presented as confirmed until it has been measured on the actual hardware. As the investigation progresses, this article will be updated from test plan to reproducible interface documentation.</p>
</article></Layout>